IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sga3-78a-78c`
IMPORT `sga3-78d-78k`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- the procedure for a reduction of share capital (ss 78B to 78K), as a regulative layer over the Boolean encodings in sga3-78a-78c.l4 and sga3-78d-78k.l4.
--
-- The steps are ONE CHAIN: each step's clock is measured from the step before it, because a HENCE starts the next clock when the earlier step is done.
-- The chain runs: the directors' solvency statement (s 78B(3), s 78C(3)); the special resolution (s 78B(1), s 78C(1)); what the company owes from the day it is passed
-- (the statement at the meeting, s 78B(4)(a), s 78C(4)(a); the copy of the solvency statement lodged with the Registrar by a public company, s 78C(3)(c); the copy of the special resolution lodged by every company, public or private, s 186(1), which for a private company is also a condition of s 78E(1)(c));
-- the statement open to creditors throughout the 6 weeks (s 78B(4)(b), s 78C(4)(b)); a creditor's application to the Court during those 6 weeks (s 78D(2));
-- the lodging with the Registrar after the end of 6 weeks and before the end of 8 weeks where no creditor applies (s 78E(1), (2));
-- where a creditor applies: the service and the notice to the Registrar (s 78D(4)), the Court's order or dismissal (s 78F(2), (3)), the notice of the order (s 78F(4)),
-- the lodging within 15 days beginning with the end of the proceedings (s 78E(3), (4)); and the Court-approved route (ss 78G to 78I).
-- The offences are BREACH lines on the duties they attach to (s 78B(5), s 78C(5), s 78F(5)) and two prohibitions (s 78H(5), s 78J).
-- The parties are the corpus's own `Party` (sg-core.l4). The gates are the existing section functions, called and not restated.
-- Where a DATE is an input of a rule, it must agree with the day of the trace (day 0 is the day the TIMELINE line names).
-- The Court has no time limit anywhere in these sections, so no clock is encoded for it.
-- A "must ... for the reduction to take effect" (s 78E, s 78I(3)) or a lodging on which the solvency requirements depend (s 78C(3)(c)) is a condition of the reduction taking effect, or of a requirement being met, and the text states no offence for it: a late or missing lodging ends FULFILLED, with the reason (what was lost, and the statute line) in a comment beside the LEST (a closed route, not a breach).
-- Convention for the procedure layer (assumed, not ruled): BREACH is kept only for a duty or a prohibition that the text lays on a named party; a power that lapses unused, a condition that is not met, a vote that fails and a route that has closed end FULFILLED. The Court is bound by ss 78F(4) to 78I, and a step it must not take (s 78I(2)) keeps BREACH BY the court.
-- Do-once duties with no number of days (s 78D(4) "as soon as possible") take the found period of the section modules as a rule-level input, `the period the standard of time allows, as found` (decided, assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md).

DECLARE `capital reduction act` IS ONE OF
    `s 78B(3)(a) and s 78C(3)(a) all the directors make the solvency statement in relation to the reduction`
    `s 78B(1) and s 78C(1) the company passes the special resolution reducing its share capital`
    `s 78B(4)(a) and s 78C(4)(a) the company makes the solvency statement available to the members at the meeting, or serves it with every copy of the resolution`
    `s 78C(3)(c) the public company lodges a copy of the solvency statement with the Registrar`
    `s 78B(4)(b) and s 78C(4)(b) the company makes the solvency statement available at its registered office for inspection free of charge by any creditor`
    `s 78B(4)(b) and s 78C(4)(b) the company withdraws the solvency statement from inspection by creditors before the end of the 6 weeks`
    `s 186(1) and s 78E(1)(c) the company lodges a copy of the special resolution with the Registrar`
    `s 78D(2) a creditor applies to the Court for the resolution to be cancelled`
    `s 78D(4)(a) the creditor serves the application on the company`
    `s 78D(4)(b) the company gives the Registrar notice of the application`
    `s 78E(1)(d) and (2) the company lodges the documents with the Registrar after the end of 6 weeks and before the end of 8 weeks`
    `s 78F(2) the Court makes an order cancelling the resolution`
    `s 78F(3) the Court dismisses the application`
    `s 78E(3)(d)(ii) and (4)(d)(ii) the creditor withdraws the application so that the proceedings end without determination`
    `s 78F(4) the company sends notice of the order to the Registrar`
    `s 78E(3)(e) and (4)(e) the company lodges the directors' statement, the copy of the Court's order and the notice containing the reduction information`
    `s 78G(1) the company applies to the Court for an order approving the resolution`
    `s 78H(2) the Court settles a list of qualifying creditors`
    `s 78I(1) the Court makes an order approving the reduction`
    `s 78I(3) the company lodges a copy of the order and a notice containing the reduction information`
    `s 78H(5) an officer conceals or misrepresents a qualifying creditor's name, debt or claim, or aids, abets or is privy to it`
    `s 78J a director makes a statement under section 78E which is false and which the director does not believe to be true`

§ `Counting helpers`

-- The period of 20 (or 30) days ending with the resolution date begins 19 (or 29) days before it (sg-periods P10).
-- A statement made on day 0 is not before the beginning of that period for any resolution date up to the last day of the period of 20 (or 30) days BEGINNING with day 0, which is day 19 (or 29).
GIVEN `the date of the solvency statement` IS A DATE
      `the number of days in the period ending with the resolution date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from the solvency statement to the latest resolution date it can serve` MEANS
    (DATE_SERIAL (`period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the date of the solvency statement` `the number of days in the period ending with the resolution date` Days)) MINUS (DATE_SERIAL `the date of the solvency statement`)

-- "the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date" end on the 41st day after it: 41 for 6 weeks, 55 for 8 weeks (sg-periods P3 and P10).
GIVEN `the resolution date` IS A DATE
      `the number of weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from the resolution date to the last day of the weeks beginning with it` MEANS
    (DATE_SERIAL (`period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the resolution date` `the number of weeks` Weeks)) MINUS (DATE_SERIAL `the resolution date`)

-- "within N days beginning with the date": the date is day 1, so the last day is N less 1 days after it (sg-periods P10).
GIVEN `the number of days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days after its first day on which a period of days beginning with that day ends` MEANS
    `the number of days` MINUS 1

-- s 78B(2) and s 78C(2) are the same dispensation, one for each kind of company.
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the company need not meet the solvency requirements under s 78B(2) or s 78C(2)` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private company`
    THEN (`s 78B(2) the company need not meet the solvency requirements` `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    ELSE (`s 78C(2) the company need not meet the solvency requirements` `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company`) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Section 78B(4)(b) and section 78C(4)(b): the statement open to creditors for 6 weeks`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the resolution date; counting="throughout the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date", the resolution date being day 1 of the 6 weeks, so the last day is day 41, computed from the DATE input `the resolution date` by sg-periods P10; the company makes the statement available on day 0 and must not withdraw it up to day 41
-- FORK: s 78B(4)(b) | "throughout the 6 weeks" is two acts, as the existing rule in sga3-78a-78c.l4 has them: make the statement available on day 0 (a MUST), then not withdraw it before day 41 (a SHANT); one act reported on day 41 would let a report made on day 1 discharge a duty that holds to day 41 | one act ("has kept the statement available throughout the 6 weeks") due on or before day 41
-- FORK: s 78B(6) | the revocation of the resolution, which ends the requirement, is not a step here: the text puts it in the passive and names no one who revokes | an act of the company that ends the duty
