GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `capital reduction act`
`s 78B(4)(b) and s 78C(4)(b) the company must keep the solvency statement open to creditors throughout the 6 weeks` MEANS
    IF `the company need not meet the solvency requirements under s 78B(2) or s 78C(2)` `the company is a private company` `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY Company `the name of the company`
         MUST `s 78B(4)(b) and s 78C(4)(b) the company makes the solvency statement available at its registered office for inspection free of charge by any creditor`
         WITHIN 0
         HENCE (PARTY Company `the name of the company`
                SHANT `s 78B(4)(b) and s 78C(4)(b) the company withdraws the solvency statement from inspection by creditors before the end of the 6 weeks`
                WITHIN (`the days from the resolution date to the last day of the weeks beginning with it` `the resolution date` 6)
                HENCE FULFILLED
                LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company withdrew the solvency statement from inspection by creditors before the end of the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date; the resolution does not become invalid by that alone, but every officer of the company who is in default is guilty of an offence (s 78B(5), s 78C(5))")
         LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not make the solvency statement available at its registered office for inspection free of charge by any creditor from the resolution date; the resolution does not become invalid by that alone, but every officer of the company who is in default is guilty of an offence (s 78B(5), s 78C(5))"

§ `Section 78F(4): the notice of the Court's order`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the Court makes the order cancelling the resolution; counting="within 15 days beginning with the date the order is made", the date being day 1, so the last day is day 14 (sg-periods P10)
-- src:9723 | (4) Where the Court makes an order under subsection (2), the
-- src:9724 | company must send notice of the order to the Registrar within 15 days
-- src:9725 | beginning with the date the order is made.
-- src:9727 | (5) If a company contravenes subsection (4), every officer of the
-- src:9728 | company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 78F(4) the notice of the order to the Registrar (src:9723-9728)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `capital reduction act`
`s 78F(4) and (5) the company must send notice of the order to the Registrar within 15 days beginning with the date the order is made` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 78F(4) the company sends notice of the order to the Registrar`
    WITHIN (`the days after its first day on which a period of days beginning with that day ends` 15)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send notice of the order to the Registrar within 15 days beginning with the date the order was made; every officer of the company who is in default is guilty of an offence (s 78F(5))"

