-- src:9616 | application has been withdrawn);
@ref s 78E(3)(d) the end of the proceedings (src:9609-9616)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the name of the creditor` IS A STRING
      `at the time the application is considered, the resolution has not been cancelled previously` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any debt or claim on which the application was based is outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the debt or claim has not been secured and the applicant does not have other adequate safeguards for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that security or other safeguards are unnecessary in view of the assets that the company would have after the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor withdraws the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `capital reduction act`
`s 78F and s 78E(3)(d): the Court decides, or the creditor withdraws` MEANS
    IF `the creditor withdraws the application`
    THEN PARTY Creditor `the name of the creditor`
         MAY `s 78E(3)(d)(ii) and (4)(d)(ii) the creditor withdraws the application so that the proceedings end without determination`
         HENCE (`s 78E(3)(e) and (4)(e) the company must lodge within 15 days beginning with the date the last proceedings end` `the name of the company`)
    ELSE (IF `s 78F(2) the Court must make an order cancelling the resolution` `at the time the application is considered, the resolution has not been cancelled previously` `any debt or claim on which the application was based is outstanding` `the Court is satisfied that the debt or claim has not been secured and the applicant does not have other adequate safeguards for it` `the Court is satisfied that security or other safeguards are unnecessary in view of the assets that the company would have after the reduction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN PARTY Court
               MUST `s 78F(2) the Court makes an order cancelling the resolution`
               HENCE (`s 78F(4) and (5) the company must send notice of the order to the Registrar within 15 days beginning with the date the order is made` `the name of the company`)
          ELSE PARTY Court
               MUST `s 78F(3) the Court dismisses the application`
               HENCE (`s 78E(3)(e) and (4)(e) the company must lodge within 15 days beginning with the date the last proceedings end` `the name of the company`))

§ `Section 78D(4): the service and the notice to the Registrar, beside the Court's decision`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the creditor applies to the Court; counting="as soon as possible" for the service and for the company's notice to the Registrar, which is silent on a day, so the period is the input `the period the standard of time allows, as found`, a number of days found by whoever applies the rule; the Court's decision is the rule called, with its own TIMELINE
-- FORK: s 78D(4) | "as soon as possible" is the section's own standard of time, so each of the two duties takes the found period as a rule-level input and ends BREACH when it runs out (decided, assumed, not ruled; the existing rules in sga3-78d-78k.l4:67-81 carry no WITHIN and no LEST, so the two layers differ here, as the notes say) | a MUST with no clock and no breach path
