      `any debt or claim on which the application was based is outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the debt or claim has not been secured and the applicant does not have other adequate safeguards for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that security or other safeguards are unnecessary in view of the assets that the company would have after the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor withdraws the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("as soon as possible") allows for these duties (the service of the application and the notice to the Registrar), found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `capital reduction act`
`s 78D(4), s 78E(3), s 78F: the service, the notice to the Registrar and the Court's decision after a creditor applies` MEANS
        ((PARTY Creditor `the name of the creditor`
          MUST `s 78D(4)(a) the creditor serves the application on the company`
          WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section's own standard: "as soon as possible" (s 78D(4)(a)); the period is an input, as found (decided, assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
          HENCE FULFILLED
          LEST BREACH BY Creditor `the name of the creditor` BECAUSE "the creditor did not serve the application on the company as soon as possible, which is the period found as an input (s 78D(4)(a))")
         RAND
         (PARTY Company `the name of the company`
          MUST `s 78D(4)(b) the company gives the Registrar notice of the application`
          WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section's own standard: "as soon as possible" (s 78D(4)(b)); the period is an input, as found (decided, assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
          HENCE FULFILLED
          LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not give the Registrar notice of the application as soon as possible, which is the period found as an input (s 78D(4)(b))"))
    RAND
        (`s 78F and s 78E(3)(d): the Court decides, or the creditor withdraws` `the name of the company` `the name of the creditor` `at the time the application is considered, the resolution has not been cancelled previously` `any debt or claim on which the application was based is outstanding` `the Court is satisfied that the debt or claim has not been secured and the applicant does not have other adequate safeguards for it` `the Court is satisfied that security or other safeguards are unnecessary in view of the assets that the company would have after the reduction` `the creditor withdraws the application`)

§ `Sections 78D and 78E(1), (2): the creditors' 6 weeks and the lodging after them`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the resolution date; counting="at any time during the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date" for the creditor (day 0 to day 41, computed from the DATE input by sg-periods P10) and "after the end of 6 weeks, and before the end of 8 weeks, beginning with the resolution date" for the company (day 42 to day 55); the lodging clock is the rest of the 8 weeks after the creditors' window lapses, which is day 55 less day 41
-- FORK: s 78E(1)(d) | the last day is day 55, so a lodging on the last day of the 8 weeks is "before the end" of them | the last day is day 54
-- FORK: s 78E(1)(c) | the copy of the resolution lodged "in accordance with section 186" is its own rule, `s 186(1) and (3), s 78E(1)(c) ...`, run beside the creditors' window for every company from the resolution date (14 days after the passing, src:16961-16963; the offence at s 186(3), src:16976-16979); the one act of this rule is the documents of paragraph (d) (and of s 78E(2)(c), (d)) (decided by Claude 2026-11-27, assumed, not ruled) | one act for the copy and the documents
-- FORK: s 78D(3) | an application by a person who is not a creditor within s 78D(3) is not an application under s 78D(2), so s 78E(1)(b) is still met and the company's lodging is still owed: it is owed from the day of that application to day 55, carried by the DATE input `the date of the application`, which must agree with the day of the trace; a lodging between that application and day 42 is accepted here although the text says "after the end of 6 weeks" | the application as one that stops the lodging under s 78E(1)(b), the rule then FULFILLED
