§ `Section 186(1) and (3), and section 78E(1)(c): the copy of the special resolution`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the resolution is passed; counting="within 14 days after the passing or making thereof", so the last day is day 14; the duty is owed by every company, public or private
-- FORK: s 186(1) | the duty is the company's own ("be lodged by the company") and s 186(3) makes a default an offence of the company and of every officer in default, so a late or missing copy is a BREACH by the company; that a private company's reduction does not take effect without it (s 78E(1)(c)) is said beside it (decided by Claude 2026-11-27, assumed, not ruled) | a bare condition of s 78E(1)(c), ending FULFILLED
-- FORK: s 186(1) | the rule is run for every company from the resolution date, public or private, whether or not s 78B(2) or s 78C(2) dispenses it from the solvency requirements: s 186(1) applies to "every special resolution" (src:16954), and s 78C(3)(c) does not provide otherwise, since it refers back to "the copy of the resolution required to be lodged with the Registrar under section 186" (src:9474-9475), so the s 78C(3)(c) act is the copy of the statement alone, and a late copy of the resolution is the s 186(3) offence of a public company too (decided by Claude 2026-11-27, assumed, not ruled) | the rule run for a private company only, with a public company's copy of the resolution folded into the s 78C(3)(c) act, whose late branch ends FULFILLED
