§ `Sections 78G to 78I: the reduction approved by the Court`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the company applies to the Court under s 78G(1); counting=silent for the Court's list, its order and the application ("no time limit"); the one clock is the company's lodging, whose day 0 is the day the order is made: "within 90 days beginning with the date the order is made, or within such longer period as the Registrar may ... allow", computed by the existing `s 78I(3) the last day ...` from the DATE inputs (the order date, whether the Registrar allowed longer, the last day of the longer period), which must agree with the days of the trace; the order date is day 0 of the clock because the HENCE restarts it when the order is made
-- FORK: s 78G(1) | the chain is not gated on the company being limited by shares, nor on s 78A(5); the caller supplies the facts (see the fork at s 78B(1)) | a gate on `s 78G(1) the company limited by shares may reduce ...`
-- FORK: s 78I(1) | where a creditor on the list stands in the way (s 78I(2)), the Court is under a SHANT and an order is a breach by the Court | the order simply not open to the Court, with no breach
-- FORK: s 78H(2) | the Court's duty to settle the list is a MUST with no clock (the text has none), and s 78H(4)(a) (ascertaining the creditors) is part of that one act | s 78H(4)(a) as a separate step
-- FORK: s 78G(1)(c) | the Registrar's recording, on which the reduction's taking effect depends, is not a step: it is an effect, not a duty with a clock | a MAY of the Registrar
-- FORK: s 78I(3) | the Registrar's allowance of a longer period is an input (a Boolean and the last day), not a step in the chain: the text gives no time for the company's application to the Registrar | a MAY of the Registrar
-- src:9736 | 78G.—(1) A company limited by shares may, as an alternative to
-- src:9737 | reducing its share capital under section 78B or 78C, reduce it in any
-- src:9738 | way by a special resolution approved by an order of the Court under
-- src:9739 | section 78I, but the resolution and the reduction of the share capital do
-- src:9740 | not take effect until —
-- src:9742 | (a) that order has been made;
-- src:9744 | (b) the company has complied with section 78I(3) (lodgment
-- src:9745 | of information with Registrar); and
-- src:9747 | (c) the Registrar has recorded the information lodged with him
-- src:9748 | or her under section 78I(3) in the appropriate register.
@ref s 78G(1) the application for the Court's approval (src:9736-9748)
-- src:9765 | (2) Upon the application to the Court, the Court is to settle a list of
-- src:9766 | qualifying creditors.
@ref s 78H(2) the list of qualifying creditors (src:9765-9766)
-- src:9815 | 78I.—(1) On an application by a company under section 78G(1),
-- src:9816 | the Court may, subject to subsection (2), make an order approving the
-- src:9821 | reduction in share capital unconditionally or on such terms and
-- src:9822 | conditions as it thinks fit.
@ref s 78I(1) the Court's order (src:9815-9822)
-- src:9824 | (2) If, at the time the Court considers the application, there is a
-- src:9825 | qualifying creditor within the meaning of section 78H —
-- src:9827 | (a) who is included in the Court’s list of qualifying creditors
-- src:9828 | under that section; and
-- src:9830 | (b) whose claim has not been terminated or whose debt has not
-- src:9831 | been discharged,
-- src:9833 | the Court must not make an order approving the reduction unless
-- src:9834 | satisfied, as respects each qualifying creditor, that —
-- src:9836 | (c) the qualifying creditor has consented to the reduction;
-- src:9838 | (d) the qualifying creditor’s debt or claim has been secured or
