@ref s 78I(3) the lodging within 90 days (src:9845-9855)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the company makes an application under section 78G(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposed reduction of share capital involves a reduction of liability in respect of unpaid share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposed reduction of share capital involves the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court so directs in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      creditors IS A LIST OF `s 78I(2) qualifying creditor`
      `the date the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has allowed a longer period on the application of the company and on receiving the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the longer period the Registrar allowed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `capital reduction act`
`s 78G to s 78I: the application to the Court, the list, the order and the lodging within 90 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MAY `s 78G(1) the company applies to the Court for an order approving the resolution`
    HENCE ((IF `s 78H(1) this section applies` `the company makes an application under section 78G(1)` `the proposed reduction of share capital involves a reduction of liability in respect of unpaid share capital` `the proposed reduction of share capital involves the payment to a shareholder of any paid-up share capital` `the Court so directs in the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN PARTY Court
                 MUST `s 78H(2) the Court settles a list of qualifying creditors`
                 HENCE FULFILLED
            ELSE FULFILLED)
           RAND
           (IF `s 78I(2) the Court must not make an order approving the reduction` creditors EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN PARTY Court
                 SHANT `s 78I(1) the Court makes an order approving the reduction`
                 HENCE FULFILLED
                 LEST BREACH BY Court BECAUSE "the Court made an order approving the reduction although a qualifying creditor on its list, with a claim not terminated or a debt not discharged, had neither consented, nor been secured or otherwise safeguarded, nor been shown to need no security (s 78I(2))"
            ELSE PARTY Court
                 MAY `s 78I(1) the Court makes an order approving the reduction`
                 HENCE (PARTY Company `the name of the company`
                        MUST `s 78I(3) the company lodges a copy of the order and a notice containing the reduction information`
                        WITHIN ((DATE_SERIAL (`s 78I(3) the last day for the company to lodge the copy of the order and the notice` `the date the order is made` `the Registrar has allowed a longer period on the application of the company and on receiving the prescribed fee` `the last day of the longer period the Registrar allowed`)) MINUS (DATE_SERIAL `the date the order is made`))
                        HENCE FULFILLED
                        LEST FULFILLED)))   -- closed route, not a breach: a lodging after the 90 days, or the longer period the Registrar allowed, means the reduction does not take effect (s 78G(1)(b), s 78I(3)); the text states no offence (src:9845-9855)

§ `Section 78H(5): concealing or misrepresenting a qualifying creditor`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the Court begins to settle the list; counting=silent (a standing prohibition; the text puts no time on it)
-- Penalty (stated in the text): a fine not exceeding $15,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years.
-- FORK: s 78H(5) | the prohibition is derived from the offence and its bearer is an officer of the company (ruling N2 of 2026-11-04) | no bearer
-- src:9793 | (5) Any officer of the company who —
-- src:9795 | (a) intentionally conceals the name of a qualifying creditor;
-- src:9797 | (b) intentionally misrepresents the nature or amount of the
-- src:9798 | debt or claim of any creditor; or
-- src:9800 | (c) aids, abets or is privy to any such concealment or
-- src:9801 | misrepresentation,
-- src:9803 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:9804 | not exceeding $15,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:9805 | 3 years.
@ref s 78H(5) the offence of concealing or misrepresenting (src:9793-9805)
GIVEN `the name of the officer` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `capital reduction act`
`s 78H(5) an officer must not conceal or misrepresent a qualifying creditor's name, debt or claim` MEANS
    PARTY Officer `the name of the officer`
    SHANT `s 78H(5) an officer conceals or misrepresents a qualifying creditor's name, debt or claim, or aids, abets or is privy to it`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Officer `the name of the officer` BECAUSE "the officer intentionally concealed the name of a qualifying creditor, or intentionally misrepresented the nature or amount of a creditor's debt or claim, or aided, abetted or was privy to it: guilty of an offence, liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $15,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years (s 78H(5))"

§ `Section 78J: a false statement to the Registrar`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the director makes the statement under s 78E(1)(d)(ii), (2)(c), (3)(e)(i) or (4)(e)(i); counting=silent (no time); the text states no penalty
-- FORK: s 78J | the offence has two elements (false, and not believed by the director to be true), and the act is one: making a statement which is both | two acts
-- src:9859 | 78J. A director making a statement under section 78E(1)(d)(ii),
-- src:9860 | (2)(c), (3)(e)(i) or (4)(e)(i) shall be guilty of an offence if the
-- src:9861 | statement —
-- src:9863 | (a) is false; and
-- src:9865 | (b) is not believed by the director to be true.
@ref s 78J the offence for a false statement (src:9859-9865)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `capital reduction act`
`s 78J a director must not make a false statement which the director does not believe to be true` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    SHANT `s 78J a director makes a statement under section 78E which is false and which the director does not believe to be true`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director made a statement under section 78E(1)(d)(ii), (2)(c), (3)(e)(i) or (4)(e)(i) which was false and which the director did not believe to be true: guilty of an offence (s 78J); the text states no penalty"

